 "title": "Eye trauma: look first for an open globe, then sort by mechanism. Surface and lid injuries are a metallic foreign body or a lid laceration; blunt trauma to the globe gives a hyphema or traumatic iritis; a stab or poke gives a corneal laceration with iris prolapse; each column gives the presentation, the exam finding and what to do",
